<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>beam_15cm</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.6">model.sdf</sdf>
  <description>
    12 ft dogbone beam course: a 3 ft x 2 ft start pad, a 6 ft long x 15 cm wide
    beam, and a 3 ft x 2 ft end pad, all 0.5 in thick with open air either side
    of the beam.  Start pad is centred on the map origin and the beam runs along
    +x with its centreline on y=0.

    meshes/beam_15cm.{stl,ply} are the SolidWorks exports
    (meshes/beam_world_15cm.{STL,PLY}) rotated into map frame; mesh coordinates
    are map coordinates, so the world include uses an identity pose.
  </description>
</model>
